WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.540 --> 00:00:02.760
- [Narrator] This is Conan and Plum.

00:00:02.760 --> 00:00:05.833
Two very still New Caledonian geckos.

00:00:06.837 --> 00:00:09.420
(upbeat music)

00:00:13.210 --> 00:00:16.570
Found exclusively in the
territory of New Caledonia,

00:00:16.570 --> 00:00:18.060
these geckos can be spotted

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:20.730
on the southern portion of the island.

00:00:20.730 --> 00:00:24.500
They have been known to grow
up to 14 inches in length.

00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:26.500
While that may not seem very big,

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:29.160
Conan and Plum are the
largest living species

00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:31.110
of gecko in the world.

00:00:31.110 --> 00:00:32.600
Typically, very calm,

00:00:32.600 --> 00:00:35.413
they only move when absolutely necessary.

00:00:37.890 --> 00:00:40.380
A greenish mossy pattern coats their body,

00:00:40.380 --> 00:00:43.130
camouflaging them in
their natural habitat.

00:00:43.130 --> 00:00:45.760
Their colors range from
a rusty red and brown

00:00:45.760 --> 00:00:47.870
to green or gray.

00:00:47.870 --> 00:00:50.880
Unlike most geckos, it
has claws on its toes

00:00:50.880 --> 00:00:53.940
and these along with a
grasping pad under the tail,

00:00:53.940 --> 00:00:55.753
help it cling to tree trunks.

00:00:56.630 --> 00:00:59.920
The primary threat to this
species is the continued loss

00:00:59.920 --> 00:01:02.863
and degradation of forest habitat.

00:01:02.863 --> 00:01:05.163
This is the New Caledonian gecko.

00:01:06.530 --> 00:01:09.113
(upbeat music)

00:01:11.279 --> 00:01:13.446
(chiming)

